nly three runners ahead. Not thirteen. Not even ten. Just three. Fourth place? His mouth went dry and his pulse quickened as the reality dawned on him. Seeing himself so close to the front, adrenaline coursed through his veins.\nAs Alex approached the final slope, his legs started to ache. He was breathing heavily as he pushed on. The cheers were thunderous, but one voice rose above the rest.\n\"You can do this, Alex!\" his coach’s familiar voice rang out. With newfound confidence, Alex surged forward, drawing on all his training. As Alex crossed the finish line, Coach Nelson pumped his fists in the air and congratulated him.\n\"I saw what you could do in training,\" Coach Nelson declared with pride, \"but today you showed me so much more. That’s the runner I knew was in there! I hope you will remember this experience, Alex — your effort got you here.\" Alex had not merely completed the race — he had excelled with hard work, finishing just behind Kai and surpassing all expectations. Kai stared at Alex, his eyes wide and mouth slightly agape. Shock was written all over his face. Then breaking into a warm, encouraging grin, Kai clapped him on the back.\n\"You’ve become such a strong runner! You are a worthy competitor,\" he said with genuine pride. \"Keep pushing like this, and soon you’ll be the one to beat!\"\n\"Thanks for believing in me,\" Alex said, smiling warmly. \"Thanks for keeping an eye on me during the race,\" Alex added. \"Those warnings about the roots really helped.\"\nThat afternoon, Alex noticed Coach Nelson conversing with a younger runner. Alex approached them. The younger runner looked up anxiously.\n\"Run your own race. It’s normal to feel nervous at first, but stay steady, trust yourself, and don’t stop,\" Alex said. He gave the younger boy a reassuring nod and added, \"You’re stronger than you think.\"\nThose were the same words Coach Nelson had said to him before the race. Back then, he doubted they applied to him. But now, after everything that had happened, Alex finally believed in them.",
